Subject: [PATCH] scripts: gen_relocate_app: objects of a module's library

Local patch of this workspace (zephyr/manifest/zephyr/patches.yml), not
meant for upstream.

zephyr_code_relocate() hands the generator the sources, and the
generator looks for each one's object in the build directory: an object
of the source's name whose directory's name contains the name of the
source's directory (drivers/i2c/i2c_dw.c in drivers__i2c.dir), or one in
app.dir. A library whose name does not contain its directory's (an
external module's, lsm6dso_local of common/drivers/lsm6dso/port/zephyr)
names the object of a source in that directory <library>.dir/<name>.obj,
and the source was left where it was, without a message. When the two
searches find nothing, the object of that name is now taken if it is
the only one.

diff --git a/scripts/build/gen_relocate_app.py b/scripts/build/gen_relocate_app.py
index cbe7422..623eb55 100755
--- a/scripts/build/gen_relocate_app.py
+++ b/scripts/build/gen_relocate_app.py
@@ -588,6 +588,13 @@ def get_obj_filename(all_obj_files, filename):
         if obj_file.name == obj_filename and obj_file.parent.name == 'app.dir':
             return str(obj_file)
 
+    # A library whose directory is not in its name (an external module's):
+    # the object of a source in that directory is <library>.dir/<name>.obj.
+    # It is the source's when no other object has its name.
+    candidates = [obj_file for obj_file in all_obj_files if obj_file.name == obj_filename]
+    if len(candidates) == 1:
+        return str(candidates[0])
+
 
 # Extracts all possible components for the input string:
 # <mem_region>[\ :program_header]:<flag_1>[;<flag_2>...]:<file_1>[;<file_2>...][,filter]
